---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import TechBadge from "../../components/TechBadge.astro";

const article = {
  title: "Building a Real-Time Collaboration Engine from Scratch",
  subtitle: "A deep dive into CRDTs, operational transforms, and the architecture decisions behind conflict-free real-time editing.",
  category: "DEVELOPMENT",
  date: "Jul 15, 2026",
  readTime: "12 min read",
  tags: ["React", "WebSocket", "CRDTs", "Yjs", "TypeScript"],
};

const related = [
  {
    title: "Optimizing React Renders at Scale",
    excerpt: "Deep dive into virtualization, memoization, and the rendering pipeline for complex UIs.",
    date: "Mar 2025",
    readTime: "8 min read",
  },
  {
    title: "Type-Safe API Layers with tRPC",
    excerpt: "How we eliminated an entire class of runtime errors by leveraging end-to-end type safety.",
    date: "Jan 2025",
    readTime: "6 min read",
  },
  {
    title: "From Monolith to Microservices",
    excerpt: "A pragmatic guide to decomposing a legacy Node.js application without rewriting everything.",
    date: "Dec 2024",
    readTime: "12 min read",
  },
];
---

<Layout title={`${article.title} — Sudi David`}>
  <Header currentPath="/blog" />

  <main>
    <section class="article-header">
      <nav class="breadcrumb-nav">
        <a href="/">~</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/blog">blog</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="current">real-time-collaboration</span>
      </nav>
      <span class="category-badge">{article.category}</span>
      <h1 class="article-title">{article.title}</h1>
      <p class="article-subtitle">{article.subtitle}</p>
      <div class="author-row">
        <div class="author-avatar">
          <img src="/Avatar.png" alt="Sudi David" width="40" height="40" />
        </div>
        <div class="author-info">
          <span class="author-name">Sudi David</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">&middot;</span>
          <span class="meta-text">{article.date}</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">&middot;</span>
          <span class="meta-text">{article.readTime}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cover-wrap">
      <div class="cover-image"></div>
    </div>

    <article class="article-body">
      <p>
        Real-time collaboration is one of those features that seems deceptively simple
        from the outside. Users type, and everyone sees the changes. But beneath the
        surface lies a fascinating set of distributed systems challenges that have
        occupied computer scientists for decades.
      </p>

      <h2>The Problem with Naive Approaches</h2>

      <p>
        The simplest approach — last-write-wins — breaks down immediately in a
        collaborative context. When two users edit the same paragraph simultaneously,
        one person's changes will be silently overwritten. This is not just a bad user
        experience; it's data loss.
      </p>

      <p>
        Operational Transform (OT) was the first serious attempt to solve this. Google
        Docs uses OT, and it works well — but it requires a central server to serialize
        operations. For our use case, we wanted something that could work peer-to-peer.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        "CRDTs guarantee that if two replicas have received the same set of updates —
        possibly in different orders — they will be in the same state. No coordination
        required."
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Enter CRDTs</h2>

      <p>
        Conflict-free Replicated Data Types solve this elegantly. Instead of
        transforming operations against each other, CRDTs define data structures where
        all concurrent operations commute — meaning the order doesn't matter. The result
        is always the same.
      </p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="code-lang">typescript</span>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <pre><code><span class="hl">interface CRDT&lt;T&gt; {'{'}</span>
  state: T;
  merge(remote: T): T;
  apply(op: Operation): T;
{'}'}

<span class="hl">class TextCRDT implements CRDT&lt;Doc&gt; {'{'}</span>
  merge(remote: Doc): Doc {'{'}
    return this.state.integrate(remote);
  {'}'}
{'}'}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Architecture Decisions</h3>

      <p>
        We chose Yjs as our CRDT library for its maturity and performance
        characteristics. The architecture consists of three layers: a thin client SDK
        that wraps Yjs, a WebSocket relay server for propagating updates, and an
        optional persistence layer backed by PostgreSQL.
      </p>

      <p>
        The relay server is intentionally stateless — it simply broadcasts updates to
        all connected clients in a room. This means horizontal scaling is trivial: spin
        up more relay servers behind a load balancer and use Redis Pub/Sub for
        cross-server communication.
      </p>

      <h3>Results & Lessons Learned</h3>

      <p>
        After six months in production, the system handles 500+ concurrent editors with
        sub-50ms sync latency. The key takeaway: CRDTs aren't magic, but they
        dramatically simplify the mental model. Instead of reasoning about operation
        ordering, you reason about data structure properties.
      </p>

      <hr class="article-divider" />

      <div class="tags-row">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12.586 2.586A2 2 0 0 0 11.172 2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414l8.704 8.704a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l6.58-6.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="7.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg>
        {article.tags.map((tag) => (
          <TechBadge label={tag} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="related-section">
      <div class="related-header">
        <h2 class="related-title">Related Articles</h2>
        <a href="/blog" class="all-articles-link">
          All articles
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="related-grid">
        {related.map((item) => (
          <a href="/blog/real-time-collaboration" class="related-card">
            <h3 class="related-card-title">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="related-card-excerpt">{item.excerpt}</p>
            <div class="related-card-meta">
              <span>{item.date}</span>
              <span>&middot;</span>
              <span>{item.readTime}</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 1440px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* ---- Article Header ---- */

  .article-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 48px 360px 32px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .breadcrumb-nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .breadcrumb-nav a {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .breadcrumb-nav a:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .sep {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .current {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .category-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-dim);
    border-radius: 9999px;
  }

  .article-title {
    font-family: "Geist", sans-serif;
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .article-subtitle {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .author-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .author-avatar {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .author-avatar img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top;
  }

  .author-info {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .author-name {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .meta-dot {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .meta-text {
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  /* ---- Cover ---- */

  .cover-wrap {
    padding: 0 120px;
  }

  .cover-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 400px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% 50%, rgba(96, 126, 188, 0.15) 0%, transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 70% 40%, rgba(96, 126, 188, 0.1) 0%, transparent 50%),
      var(--color-bg-card);
  }

  /* ---- Article Body ---- */

  .article-body {
    padding: 48px 360px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .article-body p {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .article-body h2 {
    font-family: "Geist", sans-serif;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .article-body h3 {
    font-family: "Geist", sans-serif;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .article-body blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ---- Code Block ---- */

  .code-block {
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .code-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .code-lang {
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .code-header svg {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .code-header svg:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .code-block pre {
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-block code {
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .code-block code .hl {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* ---- Divider & Tags ---- */

  .article-divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin: 8px 0;
  }

  .tags-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .tags-row svg {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  /* ---- Related Articles ---- */

  .related-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 48px 80px;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .related-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .related-title {
    font-family: "Geist", sans-serif;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .all-articles-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .all-articles-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .related-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .related-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 20px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .related-card-title {
    font-family: "Geist", sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .related-card:hover .related-card-title {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .related-card-excerpt {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .related-card-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  /* ---- Responsive ---- */

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .article-header {
      padding: 48px 120px 32px;
    }

    .cover-wrap {
      padding: 0 48px;
    }

    .article-body {
      padding: 48px 120px;
    }

    .related-section {
      padding: 48px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .article-header {
      padding: 32px 24px 24px;
    }

    .article-title {
      font-size: 28px;
    }

    .article-subtitle {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .cover-wrap {
      padding: 0 24px;
    }

    .cover-image {
      height: 240px;
    }

    .article-body {
      padding: 32px 24px;
    }

    .article-body h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    .article-body h3 {
      font-size: 18px;
    }

    .related-section {
      padding: 32px 24px;
    }

    .related-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .author-info {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
  }
</style>
